WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.230
Milady.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:12.150
It appears that your 
mind is somewhere else.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.740
If something is bothering you, 
we'd be more than happy to listen.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.500
Looking so worried isn't like you, Milady.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.790
He's an artificial human that I created.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.270
A homunculus.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.300
Princess!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.290
What is it, you two? 
Entering without knocki—

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.660
It's an emergency.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.010
What?

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.910
And more come crawling in.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.050
What's wrong? You came rushing in.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.990
Papa will wake up.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.510
Oh, sorry.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.880
Sleep is the best thing for Mondo to heal.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.690
Sleep is best?

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.680
Meaning...

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.350
Papa was just exhausted and is sleeping?

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.350
I was told it was an emergency.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.560
Well,

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.270
it's still an emergency.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.380
Since he's doing excess work

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.230
without consulting us.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.450
Don't worry, my kittens.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.590
Mama?

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.150
Leave Mondo to me.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.350
Just watch over Regalo 
like you usually do.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.170
Yeah! Leave it to me!

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.630
Even if it meant my life.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.760
You're too dramatic.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.380
You're taking this too lightly!

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:28.420
All right, don't start fighting. 
Let's go, you two.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.850
Milady, as well.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.060
A siesta at the beginning of the day.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.650
Papa is amazing.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.460
I feel like I lost in the 
contest of love for siestas.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.320
Yeah, we lost. It was a crushing defeat.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.240
Jeez.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.130
You've always had a knack 
for faking sleeping.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.330
What are we going to do with you?

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.090
Ow!

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.550
In Giappone, we call that "tanukineiri."

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.340
Ow!

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.550
Ow, ow, ow!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.880
Sumire, if you pinch that hard, 
you'll rip my butt off!

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.430
You'll become more of a 
man if I rip off a little.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.270
But, Mondo...

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.360
Are you sure this is 
how you want things?

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.160
You can stop with the useless questions.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.950
I'm not asking you.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.770
You guys,

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:35.430
this isn't something to discuss in front 
of someone who needs their rest.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.670
There's no more time.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:46.850
Meaning there's only 
one thing we should do.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.180
It's not just one.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.060
It appears that we will never agree.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.610
Despite how long we've known each other,

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:01.030
I'd have to agree with that.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.990
And we'll leave it at that.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.290
Milady.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:12.280
It looks like you have 
something you want to ask.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.570
If you're that interested,

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.670
allow us to sate that curiosity.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.630
Welcome back, Jolly.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.220
Oh, hi, Miss.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.440
He looks like a normal child, doesn't he?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.670
Despite that,

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.810
he has a contract with 
the sixteenth card,

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:48.120
La Torre: the Tower.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.950
A contract with the Tower?

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.790
I just have to listen to 
what you say, right, Jolly?

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:01.990
Exactly, Elmo. Go play outside.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.840
But she came to visit.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.720
Milady has something important 
to discuss with me.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.560
I'll be helping you if 
I listen to you, right?

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.500
Indeed.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.640
Okay.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.270
See you again, Miss.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.570
The reason Elmo was born is...

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.650
Jolly!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.400
The reason he was born?

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.980
You mean Elmo was...

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.130
Precisely, Milady.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.470
Stop!

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.910
There's nothing else to tell Milady...

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.220
Tell me.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.910
As you've figured out,

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:04.570
I've created the homunculus 
to contract with the Tarocco.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.860
Why would you have him 
contract with the Tarocco?

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.320
I will answer that question

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.970
since I am the director.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.290
Please listen carefully.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:28.480
Long ago, Mondo had undone 
the seal on the Tarocco.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.490
And then he established a contract with

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:34.510
the card, Il Mondo: The World.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.800
The World is the card that 
unifies all of the Tarocco.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.530
But there was a great consequence.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.060
A great consequence?

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.020
Even among all of the Tarocco,

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:55.260
the cards 0-22, in other 
words, the Major Arcana,

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:59.170
exist by consuming the emotional 
strength of the host.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:04.400
My Emperor, Jolly's Moon,

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.420
your Lovers...

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.340
The card doesn't matter.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:18.090
But the cards that are not 
contracted, or without hosts,

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:23.350
survive by receiving power 
from the host of the World.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:27.750
Is that the excess work 
Jolly was talking about?

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:31.300
Because of that, Mondo...

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.110
What? What's going to happen to Papa?

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:41.240
He'll soon fall into a coma, 
and eventually...

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.830
Is there any way to save Papa?

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.670
We just have to lighten Mondo's burden

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.800
by ensuring each card has a host.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.800
I had

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.100
Luca and Temperance,

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.640
Debito and the Hermit,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.350
and Pace and Strength

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.770
establish contracts together 
when they were young,

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.770
for that very reason.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.410
So, to find hosts for the remaining cards—

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.740
I told you already.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.370
Following countless experiments,

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.770
the only ones that were 
able to establish contracts

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.700
were those three.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:25.080
So that's why you made a homunculus...

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.720
No.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.590
At this point, it's nothing more than garbage.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:33.960
That's...

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.550
But there is another way to save Mondo.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.050
Jolly, stop!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.510
Is there a reason to 
hesitate at this point?

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:57.470
It's to use the other Tarocco
that you have, Milady.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.280
The Wheel of Fortune?

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:05.330
That's right. Besides the Lovers,

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:10.260
you have a contract with the tenth card,

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.340
La Ruota Della Fortuna: 
the Wheel of Fortune.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.510
But...

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.630
But?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:34.290
Papa and Mama never told me

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:37.700
exactly what powers that Tarocco holds.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:42.290
The power of the Wheel of Fortune

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:46.660
is to change the relationship 
of the host and the Tarocco.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.020
The relationship of the 
host and the Tarocco?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:54.940
You once saved Sumire with that power.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.300
Stop it, Sumire!

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.510
No! The only way left is for 
me to use my Arcana powers!

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:07.420
It's true, if we use your 
Judgment, it can heal...

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:10.730
Mondo would be 
able to recover from his illness.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.640
But there's no guarantee that the 
World won't influence Judgment,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.650
causing it to go berserk.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:22.200
Wait for me, Mondo!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.830
Culla Protezione!

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.650
Jolly, do something!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.070
There's nothing I can do.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:09.040
What's wrong, Mama?

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:17.920
It can't be...

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.110
Felicitá!

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.580
Thirteen years ago,

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.280
Sumire was saved because 
you unconsciously used

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.510
the Wheel of Fortune power.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.260
I...

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.470
don't remember anything.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:09.930
Why?

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:15.340
Because the Wheel of Fortune 
changed the relationship

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.400
between the berserk Judgment and Sumire.

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:19.500
Then...

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.150
If I use the Wheel of Fortune 
power on Papa...

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.610
There is a possibility.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:29.210
But the Wheel of Fortune—

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.210
Milady.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:34.010
Why do you think that Mondo

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:38.420
sent you away from this mansion
and only allowed you to interact

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.840
with a small group of people?

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.760
It's so you won't unconsciously use

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:48.220
the Wheel of Fortune power again.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.770
However...

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:53.680
Mondo realized that he doesn't 
have much longer to live,

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:59.650
so he summoned you back to 
spend his remaining time with you.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:04.730
And he decided to hold this 
ridiculous Arcana Duello

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:07.630
to find an heir.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:08.860
That way...

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:14.710
you'll have someone to support 
you after you lose your father.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:18.120
In two months, we will be 
holding the Arcana Duello.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.540
The winner will receive 
the title of "Papa,"

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.010
and I shall grant your wish.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.500
One more thing.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:32.680
The winner will marry 
my daughter, Felicitá.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.570
What's wrong?

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:59.960
So you heard...

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.070
Mama...

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.240
Yes?

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.760
Why did Papa choose a 
card like the World,

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:17.690
if it had such dangerous consequences?

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.900
M-Mama?

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.840
M-Mondo...

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.910
Jolly! Where are the others?

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.250
Halt!

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.740
Find and kill any member 
of the Arcana Famiglia!

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.780
You're going to use it?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.730
The power of the Tarocco?

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:13.700
Yeah.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.430
The reason I established a 
contract with the Tarocco

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.200
was for this.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.130
Mondo!

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:37.720
I am Il Mondo: the World.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:43.410
It appears that you need my powers.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.190
Yeah.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:48.860
Do you swear loyalty to us?

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:51.730
Sure.

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.820
If that means that I can 
protect those dear to me.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:17:00.160
You still have an opportunity 
to nullify the contract.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.370
Enough.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.960
I will decide my own path!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:10.010
Then shout, "Giurati Finalizzare."

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:19.660
Jolly, move away.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.060
The safest place on this 
island is right next to you.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.520
No doubt.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.210
Giurati Finalizzare!

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.510
Your father is a great person.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:39.870
And...

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.500
A tactless person.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.170
Mama...

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:49.040
I want to save Papa!

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.870
Thank you.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:56.950
Oh my...

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:08.150
If we use my Wheel of Fortune, 
we can save Papa!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.360
You found out about your powers?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.370
I had told them to never say anything.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:20.720
They're hopeless.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:22.270
I'm sorry.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.660
No, you have no reason to apologize.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.090
Listen well, Felicitá.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:37.230
Have you been able to control your 
Lovers power by your own free will?

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.220
You see?

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.980
That means that your heart 
is not strong enough

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.310
to use the Wheel of Fortune power.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.180
We will save Mondo, no matter what.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:19:02.160
So don't ever mention the 
Wheel of Fortune again.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.170
What the hell?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.570
I was all excited to see

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:20.510
how much you improved since 
you asked me to spar with you.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.180
Do you really think

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.640
that I'm actually giving it my all?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:28.350
You never shut up, do you, chickpea?

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.730
Don't call me a chickpea!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:39.700
Have you been able to control your 
Lovers power by your own free will?

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:45.580
I'm sorry, guys.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.080
Please, Lovers...

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:55.420
<i>Nova has clearly gotten better,</i>

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.230
<i>but there's no way I'm letting 
anyone else win the Duello!</i>

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.800
I'm going to win this and 
take the title of "Papa."

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.160
<i>I made a promise to Princess!</i>

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:09.600
Then...

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.100
I'll be your bride?

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:13.770
Huh?

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.900
You must think you have the edge 
if you're so absent-minded.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:18.650
That's not it!

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.270
<i>If he were to incorporate</i>

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:29.010
<i>his Arcana powers into 
his sword technique,</i>

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:32.260
<i>he'd be a worthy opponent... 
But I have no intention of losing!</i>

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.370
<i>I...</i>

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:40.090
If I were to win, 
I'll wish not to marry you.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:47.300
<i>I have a duty to set her free!</i>

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:54.480
Now I'll be able to...

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:02.540
She truly is your daughter, Mondo.

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:07.110
If it's to protect those she loves,

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:09.570
she doesn't care what happens to her.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.580
You're truly alike.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:25.130
Like how neither of you consider the pain 
you'll cause to those you leave behind.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:37.310
Why didn't you tell Milady of the 
Wheel of Fortune's consequences?

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:41.270
If she knew of the consequences,

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:45.240
there's no way she'd be 
willing to use the power.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.190
You mean you expect her to...

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:52.850
If she were to use the 
Wheel of Fortune again,

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.990
she'll lose her memory again!

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.930
You're still watching this show?

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:36.390
There's only so much time 
you should be wasting.

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:39.350
You're planning on 
watching next week, too?
